Found on reuben, 2026-11-18, while tracing k196/k250. ~/.claude/skilletor/sources-read.json is the real state file, 307558 bytes. It is keyed by the lock path of every scope a sync ever recorded (src/state.ts putSourcesRead, spec §14.3, k80), and nothing removes an entry when its checkout goes away.
Count on reuben: 762 keys, 579 of them for lock paths that no longer exist, mostly agent worktrees (<repo>/.claude/worktrees/<name>/.claude/skilletor.lock.json: rules-kuerzen 68, core-skill-laenge 24, ...); also 21 relative keys such as '.claude/skilletor.lock.json' and 14 under /tmp.
Every check and sync reads and rewrites the whole file, Node and Perl alike; with k196 it was the 13-39 s in the binary. Done when entries for vanished lock paths (and relative keys, if they are a bug) are dropped on write or by a sweep, with a test; the ~180 live entries stay.

