2026-11-18 18:03 Findings (read-only so far): check never writes sources-read.json (engine.ts check() calls only sourcesRead/unreached/renderInputs; Perl check likewise) – only sync's putSourcesRead does, so the prune goes there, no new write on the read path. Sync order: apply writes the lock (apply.ts:303), then finalLock is read, then putSourcesRead (engine.ts ~1163). A live scope CAN be without its lock file: writeLock removes the file for an empty lock (lock.ts:102), and putSourcesRead still records the sources it read – that is exactly the k80 case (a source with nothing in the lock). So 'exists' = the lock's directory (the scope's .claude dir), not the lock file. On this host both rules drop the same 579 absolute keys (0 keys have a live .claude dir but no lock). Relative keys: current code still makes them – --project-dir <relative> is passed through unresolved by both CLIs (cli.ts makeContext, CLI.pm _engine); the 21 keys are 'dbio-*/.claude/…' and '.claude/…' (--project-dir . from ~/dev and from a repo). Fix: resolve --project-dir against cwd in both CLIs.

